1. Live connector scope

Outlook Email — connected as `kevin.lelitte@admin.ox.ac.uk`.

- Read: Inbox and 63 other discoverable folders (64 total, including Inbox subfolders, Sent Items, Archive, Drafts, Junk, Deleted Items); messages, attachments, contacts, categories, mailbox profile.
- Write-capable actions exposed: draft, send, reply, forward, scheduled send, mark read/unread, move messages, set categories, create folders. No email-delete action was exposed.
- Calendar read: calendars, mailbox settings, event lists/search/fetch, availability, recurring-series and recurrence-instance endpoints. A bounded calendar-view query succeeded for 2026-07-26 through 2026-09-01. The connector documentation states a 1,825-day search limit.
- Calendar write-capable actions exposed: create, update, cancel/delete, RSVP/respond, add attachments.
- Teams read: chats, chat members, chat messages, teams/channels/channel messages, meeting recordings/transcripts.
- Teams write-capable actions exposed: create chat/channel, send chat/channel messages, reply to chat/channel messages, create/update/delete Planner tasks.
- No write action was invoked.

Calendar-view results expand recurring events into individual `occurrence` and `exception` events. Those have their own event IDs; `recurrence` is commonly null on the expanded item, so recurrence-derived status is identified by `type`, `seriesMasterId`, or `recurrence`.

2. Live ID formats

- Email: literal field `id`, returned as a Microsoft Graph-style value, e.g. `AAMkADRkYzlm...AAA=`. The connector’s returned payload used `sender.emailAddress.name` and `sender.emailAddress.address`. An attempted `internet_message_id` selection did not return either `internetMessageId` or `internet_message_id`.
- Calendar: literal fields `id` and `iCalUId`. `id` is Graph-style, e.g. `AAMkADRkYzlm...AAA=`. `iCalUId` is exposed by schema but was `null` in the live list results inspected.
- Teams: literal chat field `id`, e.g. `19:meeting_YWFm...@thread.v2` or `19:...@unq.gbl.spaces`. Canonical message routes exposed by the connector are `/chats/{chat_id}/messages/{message_id}` and `/teams/{team_id}/channels/{channel_id}/messages/{root_id}` (with `/replies/{reply_id}` for channel replies).

